{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>ועברתי [And I will pass through].</b> Like a king passing from place to place (Mekhilta), and in a single passing and in a single moment they are all struck." "<b>כל בכור בארץ מצרים [Every firstborn in the land of Egypt].</b> Even the firstborns of others who are in Egypt. And from where do we know even the firstborn of Egyptians who are in other places? Scripture says: ״לְמַכֵּה מִצְרַיִם בִּבְכוֹרֵיהֶם״ (Psalms 136)." "<b>מאדם ועד בהמה [From man to beast].</b> He who began bestiality — from him the punishment begins (Mekhilta)." "<b>ובכל אלהי מצרים [And against all the gods of Egypt].</b> Those of wood rotted, and those of metal melted and flowed to the ground (ibid.)." "<b>אעשה שפטים אני ה' [I will execute judgments, I am YHWH].</b> I Myself, and not through an agent."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {2 "Reading עֲבֵרָה as 'transgression/sin' with the Mekhilta; the reference is to bestiality, for which the Egyptian firstborn were punished first."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:37.597372242Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}